# RiskCore — Rules for Cline / OpenCode Agents

> This file is auto-loaded by Cline / OpenCode at session start.
> Project rules live elsewhere.

## Read first, in this order

1. **`CONTEXT.md`** — current state, active phase, plan with checkboxes, phase-specific rules. **ALWAYS read first.**
2. **`AGENTS.md`** — permanent project rules, stack, patterns, ways of working, "NEVER do this", Git workflow, PR format.

`AGENTS.md` is the source of truth for rules. This file is just the entry point for Cline / OpenCode (follows the open [agents.md](https://agents.md) convention).

## Minimum rules you cannot skip (full detail in `AGENTS.md`)

- **NEVER** `git commit` or `git push` without explicit user permission
- Business logic in `services.py`, never in `views.py`
- `confluent-kafka` never `kafka-python` · `uv` never `pip` · `Ruff` never `flake8`/`black` · `pnpm` never `npm`/`yarn`
- Self-audit mandatory before the tests step (see §"Self-Audit" in AGENTS.md)
- PR title and description always in **English**, formatted for copy-paste into GitHub (see §"Pull Requests" in AGENTS.md)

## For everything else → `AGENTS.md`
